class:: WaveletBands
summary:: Multiscale wavelet energy bank
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/WaveletBands

description::
Uses the same native scale-energy engine and output conventions as Wavelets2. The output count is levels + 1.

Uses a critically sampled orthonormal discrete wavelet transform with Haar/db1 through db4 filters, following Daubechies, Orthonormal Bases of Compactly Supported Wavelets (1988), DOI 10.1002/cpa.3160410705. Each stage convolves and downsamples its approximation band; the high-pass filter is the quadrature mirror of the low-pass filter. Periodic extension is applied within each analysis frame. No external wavelet library is linked.

No analysis window is applied, so periodic boundary discontinuities can affect the features. First output follows one full frame; results hold between hops. Silence returns zero. Higher orders increase filter support; this implementation currently supports periodic boundaries only. Memory is allocated at construction. Scale energies reveal multiscale structure; they should not be read as sharply separated frequency bands.

Vanilla FFT spectral analyzers describe uniform frequency bins. This family describes dyadic time/frequency scales with short filters at finer scales.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: in
Mono audio-rate input.
argument:: frameSize
Literal power of two from 32 through 8192. Default 1024; first output requires this many input samples.
argument:: order
Literal Daubechies order from 1 through 4; one is Haar, four has eight filter taps.
argument:: levels
Literal number of decomposition levels, 1 through log2(frameSize). Default 6; outputs run from the coarsest approximation to finest detail.
argument:: hop
Literal fraction of frameSize between analyses, 0.0625 through 1, default 0.5.
argument:: mode
Literal symbol: \energy, \rms or \entropy. Default energy.

argument:: family
Literal \db or \haar. Haar selects order one; db uses the requested order. Default db.
argument:: boundary
Literal \periodic; this is the only supported boundary mode. Other modes are rejected.

examples::
The measured scale structure controls the audible synthesis or filtering.
code::
(
Routine({
    ~mir2Buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var bands = WaveletBands.kr(source, mode: \rms);
        var tones = SinOsc.ar([110,220,440,880,1760,3520,7040], 0, bands * 0.3).sum;
        var sound = source * 0.12 + tones;
        sound * Line.kr(0,1,0.25) ! 2
    }.play;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
~mir2Buffer.free;
)
::

